  "word_count": 94,
  "text_content": "Emeka loved to look at the stars from the roof. One night, he decided to build a rocket from old boxes. His sister Amaka laughed, because she thought it was only a game. For two weeks, Emeka painted the boxes silver. On the last day, he climbed inside and counted down from ten. Nothing happened, but Emeka did not feel sad. He imagined flying past the moon and waving at the planets. Then Amaka joined him, and together they explored the stars. When their mother called them for dinner, they promised to fly again.",
